  "description": "Meet the DownRock\nThe DownRock is our take on a modern hardtail mountain bike. Born from our love of riding local mountain bike trails and singletrack in Melbourne, this titanium frame is suited to anything from fast flow trails to blasting down technical downhill. It's not designed for gravel or bikepacking - this bike shines when pointed downhill. The DownRock geometry is optimised around a 130 mm travel fork and is compatible with up to 150 mm.\nDrop It Like It’s hot\n\nThe seat tubes are short in order to accommodate the latest generation of long travel dropper posts (170 mm - 210 mm). This is especially advantageous on a hardtail as your legs act as the rear suspension.\n\nBalanced\n\nBottle cage mounts are placed low inside the front triangle and underneath the downtube to maintain the lowest possible centre of gravity and to give room in the front triangle for a frame bag if required.\n\nScaled Geometry\n\nFront and rear centres are scaled proportionally across the sizes in order to provide the same ride and handling characteristics across a range of rider heights. This is especially important for riders with longer inseams as it prevents the saddle from sitting too far behind above the rear wheel.\n\nRe-route it\n\nFull external Cable routing for ease of maintenance, quiet operation and maximum frame integrity (Seatpost stealth routing for dropper)\n\nDrivetrain\n1x only (no front derailleurs), Max chainring 32T at 52 mm (boost) chainline\n\nFork\nCompatible with 1⅛\" - 1.5\" tapered steerer. Frame optimised for 130 mm travel forks, compatible up to 150 mm\n\nHub spacing\nBoost 12x148 mm rear dropout, RockShox Pike fork is Boost 15x110 mm.\n\nCable routing\nFull external cable routing Seatpost stealth routing for dropper\n\nSeatpost\n31.6 seatpost, 34.9 seat clamp. Optimised around 170-210 mm dropper seatposts.\n\nTyres\n82mm tyre clearance for up to 29\" x 2.6” (66 mm)",
